82 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "ccbd1570-797c-5564-8927-e502aa05caec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162186 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186163156 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162186 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186163157 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162186 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186163158 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162186 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186163159 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162186 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162186 #edb/ref 1045 "Independence of Discrete Random Variables" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162186 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186163156 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162186 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162186 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "4373edc4-1d40-5e9a-bfe9-ecc0845c2651" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162281 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186243668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162281 #edb/ref 1069 "q-109335" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162281 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162281 #edb/ref 1071 "|  | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ |\n\nCompute $P((X,Y)\\in \\{(1,4),(1,6),(2,6)\\})$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162281 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "982b31fd-731a-56a2-a3eb-b1749eaecfdc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162281 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P((X,Y)\\in \\{(1,4),(1,6),(2,6)\\}) & =P((X,Y)=(1,4)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(1,6)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(2,6)) \\\\  & =f(1,4)+f(1,6)+f(2,6) \\\\  & =0.25+0.25+0.2 \\\\  & =0.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162304 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186246776 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162304 #edb/ref 1069 "q-110385" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162304 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162304 #edb/ref 1071 "The marginal mass functions of the independent discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ are shown below. Given that the corresponding joint probability mass function is $f(x,y),$ find $f(3,1).$\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{X}(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.5$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"50\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{Y}(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.75$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th></tr></tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162304 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d3006b2b-d3f6-5ddf-b811-934181f67f97" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162304 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162304 #edb/ref 1074 "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nTherefore, since our discrete random variables are independent, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3,1) & ={f}_{X}(3)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1) \\\\  & =0.5\\cdot 0.25 \\\\  & =0.125.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162750 #edb/ref